od guy manages to turn fortune in his  favor before being brought to his knees  again by the bad guy this is to create  the illusion to the viewer or reader  that the good guy still has a chance of  gaining the upper hand before taking it  away again there are a number of moments  in this fight that matched this  description it could be Goku's initial  solar flare and charging of the spirit  bomb it could be when the a gob cuts off  the Gena's tail but what sticks down  more than anything to me in my head was  this the spirit bomb connects with  Vegeta causing him to fly miles into the  air only to crash to the earth once  again however despite taking a lofty  amount of damage from the blast Vegeta  still rise himself enough to remain in a  dominant position the double death the  Double Down his win all fighters  involved are incapacitated on their  backs unable to move with exhaustion the  playing field has been leveled this  usually manifests due to his  split-second decision made by the good  guy or a mistake made by the bad guy  this is when Gohan falls onto the GIDA  as the Azzaro  Vegeta up until this point had been  systematically dismantling the Earth's  defenses overcoming every trap but with  the help of Goku and a miscalculation on  Vegeta sparked which he defines himself  crushed beneath an enormous loser who go  Han resulting in himself Gohan  Krillin and Goku all  down for the count until finally the  finish this is as the name suggests when  the conclusion to the fight takes place  and it just so happens to segue nicely  into the final part of this video I love  this section and I think accurate or  yama has a wonderful flair for the  dramatic - when you are writing your  conclusion you ideally want to write it  in such a way that it's not immediately  predictable to the reader or viewer this  means that when you were faced with  writing an ending to your face do not  choose the first thing that comes to  your mind don't even pick the first five  thin